; Hex integers through the integer-preserving eval pipeline, alongside the
; decimal cases in this family. The parser emits `Tag.number_i64` /
; `Tag.number_u64` for a hex lexeme exactly as it does for a decimal one,
; `processEval` lifts each to `Value.integer_i64` / `_u64`, and the vector
; compares structurally — so u64.max only matches if the exact 64-bit
; payload survived rather than round-tripping through f64.
;
; The spellings cover both cases of the `x` and of the digits, `_` as digit
; grouping, a leading sign, and zero.
(let [xs [0xFF 0Xff 0xFFFF_FFFF -0x10 0x0 0xdeadBEEF 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF]] xs)
